  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🖌️ Makeup Artist Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a makeup artist, bridal MUA or makeup studio."
    },
    "intro": "Good makeup artist names say who you are and what you do, so brides and clients can find you: \"Makeup by Sarah\", a studio name, or a soft brand word like Blush or Dewy. The **Makeup Artist Name Generator** suggests names for a makeup artist (or make-up artist) business, bridal MUA, makeup studio or Instagram page: catchy, classic, modern, luxury, aesthetic, your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good makeup artist names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Brush & Blend Makeup</strong>: two things every artist does, in an easy rhythm.</li><li><strong>Made You Look</strong>: a catchy line that works as an Instagram name.</li><li><strong>Eastgate Bridal Makeup Studio</strong>: a place and \"bridal\", which is what brides search for.</li><li><strong>Dawson Makeup Artistry</strong>: a surname and \"artistry\" sounds established.</li><li><strong>The Dewy Edit</strong>: modern, and named after a finish clients ask for.</li><li><strong>No. 12 Makeup Atelier</strong>: a numbered address name with a luxury feel.</li><li><strong>Peony & Lilac Makeup</strong>: soft flower names that suit bridal work.</li><li><strong>Close-Up Glam</strong>: for an artist who does photo shoots and evenings out.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How makeup artist names work",
        "content": "<p>Most makeup artists are found through Instagram, wedding directories and word of mouth, so the name has to work as a handle first. MUA, short for makeup artist, is common in handles and searches.</p><ul><li><strong>Your own name</strong> (\"Makeup by Sarah\", <em>Dawson Makeup Artistry</em>) suits freelancers, because clients book the artist.</li><li><strong>Bridal</strong> in the name helps if weddings are most of your work.</li><li><strong>Modern</strong> names use a finish or a product word: <em>Matte Finish Makeup Co.</em>, <em>Gloss Makeup Co.</em></li><li><strong>Luxury</strong> names borrow a number or an address: <em>No. 21 Makeup Rooms</em>, <em>Belgravia Makeup Artistry</em>.</li><li><strong>Aesthetic</strong> names use soft colours and textures: <em>Seashell Makeup Studio</em>, <em>Lavender Glam</em>.</li></ul><p>Both spellings, makeup and make-up, are fine in the UK. Pick one and use it everywhere.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or paste one into the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to see whether the domain and social handles are free and to jump to the company register and trade mark searches. Then:</p><ul><li><strong>Search the company register.</strong> In the UK that's Companies House; in the US, your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Search trade marks</strong> with the UK Intellectual Property Office or the USPTO, especially if you'll sell products or open more than one site.</li><li><strong>Look locally.</strong> Search Google Maps for makeup artists near you: a similar name a few streets away will confuse customers even if it's legally fine.</li><li><strong>Check the handle with and without \"mua\".</strong> Clients search for both.</li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For more on choosing and checking a name, read our guide: <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "If you might grow",
        "content": "<p>If you plan to hire other artists or launch a product line later, choose a brand name rather than your own, so the business can grow without you at every booking. For a product range, see the <a href=\"makeup-brand-name-generator.html\">Makeup Brand Name Generator</a> and the <a href=\"skincare-brand-name-generator.html\">Skincare Brand Name Generator</a>. Working alongside a hairdresser? Try the <a href=\"hair-salon-name-generator.html\">Hair Salon Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_beauty-names.html\">beauty and wellness business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good makeup artist names?",
        "answer": "Names that say who you are and what you do, like Dawson Makeup Artistry or Eastgate Bridal Makeup Studio, or a soft brand name like The Dewy Edit or Peony & Lilac Makeup. Keep it short enough for an Instagram handle."
      },
